\section{Console output}{

Additional RCPA4 headings are controlled by the session option
\code{RCPA4.verbose}, which defaults to \code{TRUE}. Use
\code{options(RCPA4.verbose = FALSE)} to suppress these headings, or change the
setting through \code{helpC(6)}. The setting applies for the current R session.

Thee \code{RCPA4.verbose} option does not suppress result tables, plots, messages,
warnings, errors, or interactive prompts. The option \code{RCPA4.slow = FALSE}
disables the package's optional pauses independently of verbosity.
